00:43:16.690 --> 00:43:18.360
The first question comes in

00:43:18.360 --> 00:43:21.490
from someone on my team Aaron McGyver,

00:43:21.490 --> 00:43:23.540
and it's about sports cards (indistinct).

00:43:26.270 --> 00:43:28.080
It's around really about the,

00:43:28.080 --> 00:43:29.730
with the rise of online platforms,

00:43:29.730 --> 00:43:32.653
do you as a medium blockchain,

00:43:33.630 --> 00:43:36.000
do you see that the sports card industry

00:43:36.000 --> 00:43:38.770
will become predominantly a
virtual offering in the future?

00:43:38.770 --> 00:43:41.800
And if so, how will this
impact trading value

00:43:41.800 --> 00:43:43.673
of existing physical cards?

00:43:45.000 --> 00:43:47.030
- I don't think so.

00:43:47.030 --> 00:43:51.273
At least in let's say,
the next half century?

00:43:52.310 --> 00:43:55.830
Do I think something can lose
its value as a physical item,

00:43:55.830 --> 00:43:57.640
in all shapes and form? Of course I do.

00:43:57.640 --> 00:44:01.680
I just think it's too
early for like blockchain

00:44:01.680 --> 00:44:05.150
is an unbelievable technology,

00:44:05.150 --> 00:44:08.610
and I think will have
incredible ramifications

00:44:08.610 --> 00:44:10.793
on society over the next century.

00:44:11.920 --> 00:44:14.200
But do I think that
everything gets tokenized

00:44:14.200 --> 00:44:17.270
as quickly as a lot of
blockchain enthusiasts think?

00:44:17.270 --> 00:44:18.120
The answer is no.

00:44:18.120 --> 00:44:20.600
And I, and the reason I say that is,

00:44:20.600 --> 00:44:24.130
look how far along we are
in the last half decade.

00:44:24.130 --> 00:44:29.130
Blockchain has been very
prominent for the last half decade

00:44:29.920 --> 00:44:33.370
and we still don't have anywhere close

00:44:33.370 --> 00:44:35.490
to the amount of innovation on it

00:44:35.490 --> 00:44:37.540
that I think many of us thought

00:44:37.540 --> 00:44:39.400
could be the case 5 years ago.

00:44:39.400 --> 00:44:43.797
And so I think that the
tokenization of sports cards

00:44:43.797 --> 00:44:48.480
and art, and many other
things will happen.

00:44:48.480 --> 00:44:51.680
I think that there'll be some
moments of things popping

00:44:53.130 --> 00:44:54.701
kind of similar to the way that

00:44:54.701 --> 00:44:58.740
augmented reality technology
is incredibly strong

00:44:58.740 --> 00:45:00.870
right now in the world yet

00:45:00.870 --> 00:45:03.890
we've only had Pokemon
Go be a real phenomenon

00:45:03.890 --> 00:45:05.700
in the AR world.

00:45:05.700 --> 00:45:09.260
So do I think now that
something can come along

00:45:09.260 --> 00:45:12.390
and get tokenized and do really well?

00:45:12.390 --> 00:45:14.080
Yes, but for example,

00:45:14.080 --> 00:45:15.150
and this about me now this about me now,

00:45:15.150 --> 00:45:17.470
I don't talk about or do
things that I don't believe in.

00:45:17.470 --> 00:45:21.480
If I thought that trading
cards and football stickers,

00:45:21.480 --> 00:45:24.350
which would be more European,
would lose its value,

00:45:24.350 --> 00:45:29.350
I wouldn't be buying Mbappe
rookie cards for $5,000 a piece.

00:45:30.110 --> 00:45:32.120
Why? To watch it go down in value?

00:45:32.120 --> 00:45:34.570
So I don't think in the short term,

00:45:34.570 --> 00:45:36.098
there's gonna be that level of traction.

00:45:36.098 --> 00:45:40.050
I think people underestimate
human behavior,

00:45:40.050 --> 00:45:42.220
here's what I mean by that.

00:45:42.220 --> 00:45:45.090
online dating, in the mid 90s,

00:45:45.090 --> 00:45:46.910
I told all my friends that all of them

00:45:46.910 --> 00:45:48.340
would be doing online dating

00:45:48.340 --> 00:45:51.470
if they didn't get married
before online dating.

00:45:51.470 --> 00:45:53.518
And when I tell you
everybody made fun of me,

00:45:53.518 --> 00:45:55.380
for saying that, they made fun of me,

00:45:55.380 --> 00:45:57.950
because at the time in 1996,

00:45:57.950 --> 00:46:01.100
online dating was very creepy

00:46:01.100 --> 00:46:03.490
and was really when you
thought about online dating,

00:46:03.490 --> 00:46:05.160
the image you thought about was

00:46:05.160 --> 00:46:08.290
a 600 pound guy in his mom's basement.

00:46:08.290 --> 00:46:10.100
Well, now, as we all know,

00:46:10.100 --> 00:46:13.969
online dating is
foundational to all youth,

00:46:13.969 --> 00:46:16.130
everyone for that matter.

00:46:16.130 --> 00:46:19.770
I feel the same way about physical things.

00:46:19.770 --> 00:46:21.950
I think that people think

00:46:21.950 --> 00:46:25.570
everything's going to go
on blockchain and it will.

00:46:25.570 --> 00:46:29.900
But even though online dating
is massive across the world,

00:46:29.900 --> 00:46:33.440
there is a stunning amount
of people who do not do it,

00:46:33.440 --> 00:46:34.900
and still go to the pub,

00:46:34.900 --> 00:46:36.981
or get introduced through their sister.

00:46:36.981 --> 00:46:38.910
And I think now that's what will happen

00:46:38.910 --> 00:46:42.200
in 40 years with sports cards
and other tangible goods.

00:46:42.200 --> 00:46:44.700
I think there'll be a absolute world

00:46:44.700 --> 00:46:46.850
of tokenization and blockchain,

00:46:46.850 --> 00:46:48.990
but I don't think that
will take away from people.

00:46:48.990 --> 00:46:52.100
And I would argue that
it might even enhance

00:46:52.100 --> 00:46:54.963
the value of the most rare physical items,

00:46:56.080 --> 00:46:57.670
it's what we see now.

00:46:57.670 --> 00:47:00.260
We've already seen in our
young lives, everybody here.

00:47:00.260 --> 00:47:03.880
The growth and creation
of social networks,

00:47:03.880 --> 00:47:08.190
the slow but steady curve of
people spending time on it.

00:47:08.190 --> 00:47:11.790
And now the apex moments of it so much so,

00:47:11.790 --> 00:47:15.640
that kids predominantly in their teens

00:47:15.640 --> 00:47:19.750
are taking week or month breaks from it

00:47:21.210 --> 00:47:24.190
because they're the counterculture to it.

00:47:24.190 --> 00:47:25.940
Much like the rise of blockchain

00:47:25.940 --> 00:47:28.567
will actually create tokenization of items

00:47:28.567 --> 00:47:33.460
and then you'll see people
want to own the physical card

00:47:33.460 --> 00:47:34.660
because everything went digital.

00:47:34.660 --> 00:47:36.760
No different than hipsters in Brooklyn,

00:47:36.760 --> 00:47:38.610
wanting to own pagers

00:47:38.610 --> 00:47:40.840
and flip phones instead of the iPhone.

00:47:40.840 --> 00:47:44.580
The human race likes to swing pendulums,

00:47:44.580 --> 00:47:46.290
and over the next century will swing

00:47:46.290 --> 00:47:48.960
to the digitalization of physical goods,

00:47:48.960 --> 00:47:50.800
only to then be countered,

00:47:50.800 --> 00:47:53.730
with people going backwards
into physical goods,

00:47:53.730 --> 00:47:56.310
just like what's happening
with food habits.

00:47:56.310 --> 00:47:57.910
I hope everybody
understands what's happening

00:47:57.910 --> 00:48:00.080
with food in the world.

00:48:00.080 --> 00:48:02.160
People are starting to eat clean,

00:48:02.160 --> 00:48:04.603
the way that people ate 150 years ago.

00:48:06.350 --> 00:48:08.340
We then had the rise of modern food,

00:48:08.340 --> 00:48:10.310
and Business and Technology,

00:48:10.310 --> 00:48:12.690
create all the things we've known

00:48:12.690 --> 00:48:14.080
and now people are trying to go back

00:48:14.080 --> 00:48:16.563
to just ingredients and clean eating.

00:48:16.563 --> 00:48:18.473
So that's just how humans work.

