00:49:03.744 --> 00:49:05.560
Then I was a bad student.

00:49:05.560 --> 00:49:07.160
So all my teachers said

00:49:07.160 --> 00:49:10.460
no you're failure, bad push against.

00:49:10.460 --> 00:49:13.770
I wasn't, after about
third or fourth grade,

00:49:13.770 --> 00:49:17.130
I it was clear to me that I
was not remarkable at sports.

00:49:17.130 --> 00:49:20.720
So, there wasn't that thing
that a lot of kids rely on.

00:49:20.720 --> 00:49:22.820
So I basically lived the life with

00:49:22.820 --> 00:49:25.540
a lot of adversity and a lot of no,

00:49:25.540 --> 00:49:26.837
my parents couldn't buy me things.

00:49:26.837 --> 00:49:27.887
"Mom, I want Nintendo."

00:49:27.887 --> 00:49:28.980
"No."

00:49:28.980 --> 00:49:31.210
Like, my life was about no.

00:49:31.210 --> 00:49:34.570
And so it was very easy
once I became an adult

00:49:34.570 --> 00:49:36.820
to be comfortable in no.

00:49:36.820 --> 00:49:40.110
For a lot of you, my children included,

00:49:40.110 --> 00:49:42.713
no was, you were in the business of yes.

00:49:44.020 --> 00:49:46.320
And in that became the vulnerability

00:49:46.320 --> 00:49:49.410
because no seemed scary, foreign.

00:49:49.410 --> 00:49:51.850
I think the biggest way for you

00:49:51.850 --> 00:49:54.010
or anybody else at a more advanced age

00:49:54.010 --> 00:49:55.690
of not being a child anymore,

00:49:55.690 --> 00:50:00.160
is getting into the practice
of losing and doing nos.

00:50:00.160 --> 00:50:02.143
Trying things that are hard to you,

00:50:03.280 --> 00:50:05.823
doing things that require no.

00:50:06.740 --> 00:50:09.860
People need to have a
relationship with no.

00:50:09.860 --> 00:50:13.600
And that is only something that either you

00:50:13.600 --> 00:50:16.430
are serendipitously growing up with,

00:50:16.430 --> 00:50:20.500
and or something that you
manufacture for yourself

00:50:20.500 --> 00:50:22.290
when you get older by putting yourself

00:50:22.290 --> 00:50:24.260
in uncomfortable positions,

00:50:24.260 --> 00:50:26.903
so that you become more
comfortable with rejection.

